Chr4	Araport11	gene	2452664	2457767	.	+	.	ID=AT4G04850;Name=AT4G04850;Note=K+ efflux antiporter 3;curator_summary=Encodes a potassium efflux antiporter has three splice forms KEA3.1, KEA3.2, and KEA3.3, KEA3.2 is the most abundant splice form in all plant organs (silique, flower, leaf and root).  KEA3.1 and KEA3.3 are minor variants that can be found in flowers and in leaves. KEA3 is localized to the thylakoid membrane and  enriched in the stromal lamellae. It allows proton efflux from the thylakoid lumen by proton/potassium antiport.;computational_description=K+ efflux antiporter 3;locus=2138942;locus_type=protein_coding
