Chr4	Araport11	gene	9402898	9406136	.	+	.	ID=AT4G16730;Name=AT4G16730;Note=terpene synthase 02;curator_summary=In the Col ecotype, no functional protein is encoded at this locus due to the presence of a two-base (AT) insertion 184 nucleotides  downstream of the start codon leading to a  frame shift and premature translational termination. However, in the Ws ecotype, a functional terpene synthase that localizes to the chloroplast is encoded at this locus. It can catalyze the synthesis of (E)-beta-ocimene and (E,E)-alpha farnesene in vitro, but, it has more activity as an (E)-beta-ocimene synthase activity in vivo. This may reflect the greater availability of the GPP precursor of (E)-beta-ocimene than of the FPP precursor of (E,E)-alpha-farnesene in the chloroplasts where the Ws TPS02 is present.;computational_description=terpene synthase 02;locus=2129091;locus_type=protein_coding
