Chr4	Araport11	gene	10046287	10049438	.	-	.	ID=AT4G18140;Name=AT4G18140;Note=SCP1-like small phosphatase 4b;curator_summary=Encodes a SCP1-like small phosphatase (SSP).  Three SSPs form a unique group with long N-terminal extensions: AT5G46410 (SSP4), AT5G11860 (SSP5), AT4G18140 (SSP4b). SSP4 and SSP4b were localized exclusively in the nuclei, whereas SSP5 accumulated in both nuclei and cytoplasm. All three SSPs encodes active CTD phosphatases like animal SCP1 family proteins, with distinct substrate specificities: SSP4 and SSP4b could dephosphorylate both Ser2-PO(4) and Ser5-PO(4) of CTD, whereas SSP5 dephosphorylated only Ser5-PO(4).;computational_description=SCP1-like small phosphatase 4b;locus=2117661;locus_type=protein_coding
Chr4	Araport11	mRNA	10046287	10049438	.	-	.	ID=AT4G18140.4;Parent=AT4G18140;Note=SCP1-like small phosphatase 4b;computational_description=SCP1-like small phosphatase 4b;curator_summary=Encodes a SCP1-like small phosphatase (SSP).  Three SSPs form a unique group with long N-terminal extensions: AT5G46410 (SSP4), AT5G11860 (SSP5), AT4G18140 (SSP4b). SSP4 and SSP4b were localized exclusively in the nuclei, whereas SSP5 accumulated in both nuclei and cytoplasm. All three SSPs encodes active CTD phosphatases like animal SCP1 family proteins, with distinct substrate specificities: SSP4 and SSP4b could dephosphorylate both Ser2-PO(4) and Ser5-PO(4) of CTD, whereas SSP5 dephosphorylated only Ser5-PO(4).
