Chr4	Araport11	gene	15306544	15309035	.	+	.	ID=AT4G31580;Name=AT4G31580;Note=serine/arginine-rich 22;curator_summary=Encodes a Serine/arginine-rich (SR) protein RSZp22.  SR proteins are splicing regulators that share a modular structure consisting of one or two N-terminal RNA recognition motif domains and a C-terminal RS-rich domain.  RSZp22 is located in the nucleolus. It is a nucleocytoplasmic shuttling protein and an interacting partner to the Arabidopsis U1-70K. Barta et al (2010) have proposed a nomenclature for Serine/Arginine-Rich Protein Splicing Factors (SR proteins): Plant Cell. 2010, 22:2926.;computational_description=serine/arginine-rich 22;locus=2124799;locus_type=protein_coding
